AVAR Kantar — Third-Party Software Licenses
============================================

This folder contains the full, unmodified license texts of the
open-source components used by AVAR Kantar. All rights of the
respective components belong to their original authors.

The application itself (AVAR Kantar) is proprietary; the licenses
below apply ONLY to the specific third-party components listed.

Components and their licenses
-----------------------------

  * Qt for Python (PySide6) — LGPLv3
      → LGPL-3.0.txt (and GPL-3.0.txt, referenced by the LGPL)
      Qt is used dynamically via separate DLLs shipped alongside the
      program (folder: AVAR Kantar/PySide6/*). These DLLs may be
      replaced by the end user with LGPL-compatible builds obtained
      from the Qt Project. AVAR Kantar has NOT modified Qt.

  * SQLCipher (community edition) — 3-clause BSD
      → sqlcipher-LICENSE.txt

  * openpyxl — MIT
      → openpyxl-LICENSE.txt

  * pyserial — 3-clause BSD
      → pyserial-LICENSE.txt

  * pywin32 — PSF-derived BSD
      → pywin32-LICENSE.txt

  * Lucide Icons — ISC (with historical MIT contributions)
      → lucide-LICENSE.txt

  * OpenSSL (bundled with SQLCipher/Python) — Apache 2.0
      → openssl-LICENSE.txt / Apache-2.0.txt

  * Python — PSF License 2.0
      → PSF-2.0.txt

Where to obtain sources
-----------------------

Sources for every LGPL / GPL-covered component are available from
the upstream project pages, e.g.:
  * Qt / PySide6  — https://www.qt.io/  |  https://pypi.org/project/PySide6/
  * Python        — https://www.python.org/
  * OpenSSL       — https://www.openssl.org/
  * SQLCipher     — https://www.zetetic.net/sqlcipher/
